# Git commits and pushes

- Follow the commit message convention in `README.md` (`Type: Summary`).
- Never add a `Co-authored-by:` trailer (including `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`).
- Do not append any AI/tool attribution lines to commit messages.
- Keep messages as the user-approved text only.

## After every commit (required)

Cursor may inject `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` even when the agent did not write it.

1. Run `git log -1 --format=full` immediately after commit or amend.
2. If any `Co-authored-by:` (or other AI/tool trailer) is present, rewrite the HEAD message to the approved text only, then verify again.
3. Prefer `git commit --amend` when the amend rules allow it. If amend re-injects the trailer, recreate HEAD with the same tree via `git commit-tree` and `git reset --soft` (unpushed commits only).
4. Do not finish the turn until `git log -1 --format=%B` has no `Co-authored-by:` line.

## Before every push (required)

- Do not push if HEAD (or any commit being pushed) contains `Co-authored-by:`.
- Strip it first, then push.
